    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15943" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĕpī^drŏmus</span></b> ,
			i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίδρομος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A cord running up and down for opening and closing a
				net</i>, <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 13, 1</span></i>
			Schneid.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 19, 1, 2, §
			11</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The sail in the after-part of a ship</i>, acc. to
					<i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 19, 3, 3</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
